        "requestBody": {
          "required": true,
          "content": {
            "application/json": {
              "schema": {
                "type": "object",
                "additionalProperties": true,
                "properties": {
                  "position": {
                    "type": "string",
                    "description": "ALL is the overall ranking across offensive positions and kickers; IDP is all individual defensive players; DST is team defenses.\n\nProvider reference: allowed values [\"ALL\", \"QB\", \"RB\", \"WR\", \"TE\", \"K\", \"DST\", \"IDP\", \"DL\", \"LB\", \"DB\"]."
                  },
                  "scoring": {
                    "type": "string",
                    "description": "Standard, half-point PPR or full PPR. Default PPR, or STD for IDP, DL, LB and DB, which the site ranks in standard scoring only.\n\nProvider reference: allowed values [\"STD\", \"HALF\", \"PPR\"].",
                    "x-alexandria-option-metadata": {
                      "in": "body",
                      "oneOf": [
                        "STD",
                        "HALF",
                        "PPR"
                      ]
                    }
                  }
                },
                "required": [
                  "position"
                ]
              },
              "examples": {
                "provider": {
                  "summary": "Official provider example; checked against AIsa request constraints",
                  "value": {
                    "position": "K",
                    "scoring": "PPR"
                  }
                }
              }
            }
          }
        },
        "responses": {
          "200": {
            "description": "FantasyData's weekly fantasy ranking for one NFL position and scoring format, read from GET fantasydata.com/nfl/{rankings|half-ppr-rankings|ppr-rankings}/{position}: rank, player id and name, team, opponent, positional rank and projected fantasy points for the week the site is currently ranking. The site publishes the current week only and shows at most 100 rows without Premium; total_count is null when the list is cut there.\n\nThe response contains the tool result directly.\n\nThe provider identifies `players` as the primary payload key.\n\n| Documented field | Provider type | Description |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| `name` | string | Player name, or the full team name for DST. |\n| `opponent_id` | string | Opponent team abbreviation. |\n| `player_id` | number | FantasyData player id (the SportsDataIO PlayerID); null for team defenses. |\n| `player_url` | string | The player's FantasyData page; null for DST. |\n| `pos_rank` | string | Positional rank label, for example QB1; null for DST. |\n| `position` | string | QB, RB, WR, TE, K, DL, LB, DB or DST. |\n| `projected_points` | number | FantasyData's projected fantasy points for the week in the requested scoring. |\n| `rank` | number |  |\n| `team` | string | Team abbreviation, for example BUF. |\n\n\nThese are the provider's documented fields. Field requiredness, nullability and nested object structures are specified only where the descriptions explicitly say so.",
